menu "Servo driver (servo)"

    config SERVO_TASK_STACK_IN_PSRAM
        bool "Servo task stack in PSRAM"
        depends on SPIRAM
        default n
        help
            The frame task's 4 KB stack from PSRAM instead of internal RAM. Safe only
            while nothing on the task touches flash: every flash operation, reads
            included, asserts an internal stack. The task flushes the controllers over
            I2C, runs Servo::Tick() and calls the output listener; settings are loaded
            and saved on the callers of the C API, never here. An application whose
            output listener reads or writes NVS must leave this off. The I2C traffic is
            fine, because the I2C interrupt is not IRAM-safe (CONFIG_I2C_ISR_IRAM_SAFE)
            and so never runs while the cache is off.

endmenu
